-> start

=== start ===
Rabbi, look! The tree You cursed yesterday... it's completely withered! From the roots up!
+ [It happened so fast.]
    I've seen blights take a season to kill a tree, but this? This was overnight. One word from the Master and life just... departed.
    -> miracle
+ [Why did He curse it?]
    Because it was a liar, friend. It stood there with its leaves spread wide, promising fruit to a hungry man, but it was empty inside.
    -> judgment

=== miracle ===
It makes you realize who we're really walking with. He didn't just teach us a lesson; He showed us He has authority over the very earth we stand on.
+ [What did He say about the mountain?]
    He said if we have faith and do not doubt, we could tell this mountain to throw itself into the sea. I'm starting to think He wasn't exaggerating.
    -> faith

=== faith ===
"Have faith in God," He told us. It sounds simple, but watching that tree turn to dust... it's a heavy kind of simple. 
-> END

=== judgment ===
The Master is entering Jerusalem to face the leaders. That tree is a mirror. It looks healthy from a distance, just like the Temple rituals, but there's no fruit for God there.
-> END